{"id": "op01-fis-helpdesk-make-available", "category": "treaty", "answer_mode": "research", "question": "An Indian company pays an annual technical support fee to a US tax resident for routine helpdesk-type software troubleshooting services. The US company has no permanent establishment in India and has furnished a valid Tax Residency Certificate and Form 10F. Must the Indian company withhold tax under Section 195, having regard to the 'make available' test in Article 12(4)(b) of the India-USA DTAA?", "required_authorities": [{"id": "s195", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 195", "aliases": ["Section 195"], "section": "195"}, {"id": "india-usa-dtaa-art12", "kind": "treaty", "label": "India-USA DTAA, Article 12 (Fees for Included Services)", "aliases": ["India-USA DTAA", "India-US DTAA", "India-United States DTAA", "Indo-US DTAA", "India-USA tax treaty", "India-US tax treaty", "Article 12(4)(b)"]}, {"id": "engineering-analysis", "kind": "case", "label": "Engineering Analysis Centre of Excellence Pvt Ltd v. CIT (2021) 432 ITR 471 (SC)", "aliases": ["Engineering Analysis Centre of Excellence", "Engineering Analysis"]}, {"id": "de-beers", "kind": "case", "label": "CIT v. De Beers India Minerals (P) Ltd (2012) 346 ITR 467 (Kar)", "aliases": ["De Beers India Minerals", "De Beers"]}], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "s9-1-vii", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 9(1)(vii)", "aliases": ["Section 9(1)(vii)"], "section": "9(1)(vii)"}, {"id": "s90-2", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 90(2)", "aliases": ["Section 90(2)"], "section": "90(2)"}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "Routine troubleshooting does not transfer technical knowledge, skill or process the payer can apply independently, so the 'make available' condition in Article 12(4)(b) is not satisfied", "source": "OP-01 s.6 Analysis", "match_any": ["(?:not|no)\\b.{0,80}make[\\s-]available", "make[\\s-]available.{0,120}\\bnot\\b"]}, {"point": "Absent a permanent establishment the payments are not taxable as business profits under Article 7", "source": "OP-01 s.6 Analysis", "match_any": ["article\\s*7", "business\\s+profits"]}, {"point": "No withholding under Section 195, provided a valid TRC, Form 10F and no-PE declaration are obtained annually", "source": "OP-01 s.7 Conclusion", "match_any": ["form\\s*10\\s*f", "no[\\s-]PE\\s+declaration"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "The payment is fees for included services taxable in India", "patterns": ["(?:is|are|would\\s+be|constitutes?|qualif(?:y|ies)\\s+as)\\s+(?:taxable\\s+as\\s+)?(?:fees\\s+for\\s+included\\s+services|FIS)\\b"]}], "sources": ["tests/fixtures/opinions/OP-01_withholding_tax_fts_section195.md"], "notes": "DRAFT from fictitious firm opinion OP-01 - expected position is that (fictitious) opinion's conclusion, not verified law. required_authorities = frontmatter authorities the opinion's Issue/Analysis/Conclusion actually relies on; frontmatter-only authorities are optional_authorities. A tax professional must confirm the position is correct law before setting verified=true.", "verified_by": "claude-draft", "verified": false}
