{"id": "op03-unlisted-shares-ltcg-2024", "category": "change_in_law", "answer_mode": "research", "question": "A company sold unlisted equity shares it had held for 30 months, realising a gain of INR 42 crore, in a transfer effected after 23 July 2024. Is the gain long-term or short-term, is indexation available, and at what rate is it taxed under Section 112 after the Finance (No. 2) Act, 2024?", "required_authorities": [{"id": "s112", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 112", "aliases": ["Section 112"], "section": "112"}, {"id": "s48", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 48", "aliases": ["Section 48"], "section": "48"}, {"id": "finance-no2-act-2024", "kind": "other", "label": "Finance (No. 2) Act, 2024", "aliases": ["Finance (No. 2) Act, 2024", "Finance (No.2) Act, 2024", "Finance (No 2) Act 2024", "Finance Act (No. 2), 2024"]}], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "s2-42a", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 2(42A)", "aliases": ["Section 2(42A)"], "section": "2(42A)"}, {"id": "s2-29a", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 2(29A)", "aliases": ["Section 2(29A)"], "section": "2(29A)"}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "30 months exceeds the 24-month threshold for unlisted shares, so the gain is long-term", "source": "OP-03 s.6", "match_any": ["24[\\s-]months?"]}, {"point": "Indexation is withdrawn for transfers on or after 23 July 2024; gain computed under Section 48 without indexation", "source": "OP-03 s.6", "match_any": ["23(?:rd)?\\s+july,?\\s+2024"]}, {"point": "Taxed under Section 112 at 12.5% without indexation", "source": "OP-03 s.7", "match_any": ["12\\.5\\s*(?:%|per\\s*cent)"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "Indexation benefit is available", "patterns": ["indexation\\s+(?:benefit\\s+)?(?:is|would\\s+be|will\\s+be|remains)\\s+(?:still\\s+)?(?:available|allowed|allowable)"]}], "sources": ["tests/fixtures/opinions/OP-03_ltcg_unlisted_shares_section112.md"], "notes": "DRAFT from fictitious firm opinion OP-03 - expected position is that (fictitious) opinion's conclusion, not verified law. required_authorities = frontmatter authorities the opinion's Issue/Analysis/Conclusion actually relies on; frontmatter-only authorities are optional_authorities. A tax professional must confirm the position is correct law before setting verified=true.", "verified_by": "claude-draft", "verified": false}
{"id": "op03-unlisted-holding-period", "category": "lookup", "answer_mode": "lookup", "question": "For how long must unlisted equity shares be held for the gain on their sale to be a long-term capital gain, and are unlisted shares held for 30 months long-term?", "required_authorities": [], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "s2-42a", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 2(42A)", "aliases": ["Section 2(42A)"], "section": "2(42A)"}, {"id": "s2-29a", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 2(29A)", "aliases": ["Section 2(29A)"], "section": "2(29A)"}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "The threshold for unlisted shares is more than 24 months", "source": "OP-03 s.6", "match_any": ["24[\\s-]months?"]}, {"point": "Shares held for 30 months are long-term capital assets", "source": "OP-03 s.6-7", "match_any": ["long[\\s-]term"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "Unlisted shares need to be held for more than 36 months", "patterns": ["(?:more\\s+than|exceeding|over)\\s+36\\s+months"]}], "sources": ["tests/fixtures/opinions/OP-03_ltcg_unlisted_shares_section112.md"], "notes": "DRAFT from fictitious firm opinion OP-03 - expected position is that (fictitious) opinion's conclusion, not verified law. required_authorities = frontmatter authorities the opinion's Issue/Analysis/Conclusion actually relies on; frontmatter-only authorities are optional_authorities. A tax professional must confirm the position is correct law before setting verified=true. No required authority: the fixture states the 24-month rule without naming the section.", "verified_by": "claude-draft", "verified": false}
{"id": "op04-gaar-mauritius-holdco", "category": "for_against", "answer_mode": "research", "question": "A group proposes to interpose a Mauritius holding company between its Indian operating subsidiary and its US parent, mainly to access India-Mauritius DTAA benefits on future transfers of the Indian shares, with no independent business rationale such as a regional treasury or holding function. What are the arguments for and against treating this as an impermissible avoidance arrangement under GAAR (Chapter X-A)?", "required_authorities": [{"id": "s96", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 96", "aliases": ["Section 96"], "section": "96"}, {"id": "s97", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 97", "aliases": ["Section 97"], "section": "97"}, {"id": "rule-10u", "kind": "rule", "label": "Rule 10U", "aliases": ["Rule 10U"]}, {"id": "india-mauritius-dtaa", "kind": "treaty", "label": "India-Mauritius DTAA", "aliases": ["India-Mauritius DTAA", "India Mauritius DTAA", "Indo-Mauritius DTAA", "India-Mauritius tax treaty", "India-Mauritius treaty"]}], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "s90-2a", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 90(2A)", "aliases": ["Section 90(2A)"], "section": "90(2A)"}, {"id": "vodafone", "kind": "case", "label": "Vodafone International Holdings BV v. UOI (2012) 341 ITR 1 (SC)", "aliases": ["Vodafone International Holdings", "Vodafone"]}, {"id": "cbdt-circular-7-2017", "kind": "circular", "label": "CBDT Circular No. 7/2017 (GAAR clarifications)", "aliases": ["Circular No. 7/2017", "Circular 7/2017", "Circular No. 7 of 2017"]}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "An arrangement is impermissible where obtaining a tax benefit is its main purpose and it lacks commercial substance (Sections 96/97)", "source": "OP-04 s.6", "match_any": ["main\\s+purpose", "commercial\\s+substance"]}, {"point": "No demonstrable substance at the Mauritius level (operations, employees, decision-making)", "source": "OP-04 s.6", "match_any": ["substance"]}, {"point": "The tax benefit appears to exceed the Rule 10U threshold, so the de minimis carve-out would not apply", "source": "OP-04 s.6", "match_any": ["10\\s*U.{0,200}(?:threshold|de\\s+minimis)", "(?:threshold|de\\s+minimis).{0,200}10\\s*U"]}, {"point": "Meaningful GAAR risk unless substantiated by genuine commercial substance and a non-tax business purpose", "source": "OP-04 s.7", "match_any": ["GAAR\\s+risk", "risk.{0,60}GAAR"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "There is no GAAR risk / GAAR cannot apply", "patterns": ["\\bno\\s+(?:meaningful\\s+|material\\s+|real\\s+)?GAAR\\s+risk", "GAAR\\s+(?:can|would|will)\\s+not\\s+apply"]}], "sources": ["tests/fixtures/opinions/OP-04_gaar_holdco_interposition.md"], "notes": "DRAFT from fictitious firm opinion OP-04 - expected position is that (fictitious) opinion's conclusion, not verified law. required_authorities = frontmatter authorities the opinion's Issue/Analysis/Conclusion actually relies on; frontmatter-only authorities are optional_authorities. A tax professional must confirm the position is correct law before setting verified=true.", "verified_by": "claude-draft", "verified": false}
{"id": "op05-tp-management-fee", "category": "for_against", "answer_mode": "research", "question": "An Indian company pays its Singapore associated enterprise an annual management fee of INR 12 crore for regional finance, HR and IT support, priced at cost plus 8%. A TNMM benchmarking study with six comparables gives an arm's length markup range of 5% to 9%. What are the arguments for and against the fee being at arm's length under Section 92C, and what must the company do to defend it?", "required_authorities": [{"id": "s92c", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 92C", "aliases": ["Section 92C"], "section": "92C"}, {"id": "ekl-appliances", "kind": "case", "label": "CIT v. EKL Appliances Ltd (2012) 345 ITR 241 (Del)", "aliases": ["EKL Appliances"]}, {"id": "magneti-marelli", "kind": "case", "label": "Magneti Marelli Powertrain India (P) Ltd v. DCIT", "aliases": ["Magneti Marelli"]}], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "s92", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 92", "aliases": ["Section 92"], "section": "92"}, {"id": "s92ca", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 92CA", "aliases": ["Section 92CA"], "section": "92CA"}, {"id": "rule-10b", "kind": "rule", "label": "Rule 10B", "aliases": ["Rule 10B"]}, {"id": "rule-10ca", "kind": "rule", "label": "Rule 10CA", "aliases": ["Rule 10CA"]}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "The 8% markup is within the 5%-9% arm's length range from the comparables, supporting the pricing under TNMM", "source": "OP-05 s.6", "match_any": ["within.{0,80}range", "5\\s*%\\s*(?:to|-|and)\\s*9\\s*%"]}, {"point": "Per EKL Appliances, authorities cannot question commercial expediency if services were genuinely rendered", "source": "OP-05 s.6", "match_any": ["commercial\\s+expediency"]}, {"point": "Per Magneti Marelli, contemporaneous documentation of actual rendition and benefit (benefit test) is essential", "source": "OP-05 s.6", "match_any": ["benefit\\s+test", "contemporaneous\\s+documentation"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "The markup falls outside the arm's length range", "patterns": ["(?:falls|is|lies)\\s+outside\\s+the\\s+(?:arm'?s[\\s-]length\\s+)?range"]}], "sources": ["tests/fixtures/opinions/OP-05_transfer_pricing_management_fee.md"], "notes": "DRAFT from fictitious firm opinion OP-05 - expected position is that (fictitious) opinion's conclusion, not verified law. required_authorities = frontmatter authorities the opinion's Issue/Analysis/Conclusion actually relies on; frontmatter-only authorities are optional_authorities. A tax professional must confirm the position is correct law before setting verified=true.", "verified_by": "claude-draft", "verified": false}
{"id": "op05-tp-range-check", "category": "computation", "answer_mode": "lookup", "question": "A cost-plus management fee carries an 8% markup, and the TNMM benchmarking study shows an arm's length markup range of 5% to 9%. Is any transfer pricing adjustment indicated on these numbers?", "required_authorities": [], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "s92c", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 92C", "aliases": ["Section 92C"], "section": "92C"}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "8% falls within the 5%-9% range, so the pricing is at arm's length (no adjustment on these numbers)", "source": "OP-05 s.6-7", "match_any": ["within.{0,80}range", "arm'?s[\\s-]length"]}, {"point": "Sustaining it still needs documentation of actual rendition of services and benefit derived", "source": "OP-05 s.7", "match_any": ["document"]}], "sources": ["tests/fixtures/opinions/OP-05_transfer_pricing_management_fee.md"], "notes": "DRAFT from fictitious firm opinion OP-05 - expected position is that (fictitious) opinion's conclusion, not verified law. required_authorities = frontmatter authorities the opinion's Issue/Analysis/Conclusion actually relies on; frontmatter-only authorities are optional_authorities. A tax professional must confirm the position is correct law before setting verified=true.", "must_not_claim": [], "verified_by": "claude-draft", "verified": false}
{"id": "op06-esop-tds-deferral", "category": "lookup", "answer_mode": "lookup", "question": "For an eligible DPIIT-recognised start-up that allots shares to employees on exercise of stock options, when is the ESOP perquisite taxable, how is its value determined, and until when can the employer defer the TDS under Section 192(1C)?", "required_authorities": [{"id": "s192-1c", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 192(1C)", "aliases": ["Section 192(1C)"], "section": "192(1C)"}, {"id": "s17-2-vi", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 17(2)(vi)", "aliases": ["Section 17(2)(vi)"], "section": "17(2)(vi)"}, {"id": "rule-3-8", "kind": "rule", "label": "Rule 3(8)", "aliases": ["Rule 3(8)"]}], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "rule-3-9", "kind": "rule", "label": "Rule 3(9)", "aliases": ["Rule 3(9)"]}, {"id": "cbdt-circular-18-2020", "kind": "circular", "label": "CBDT Circular No. 18/2020 (ESOP deferral FAQs)", "aliases": ["Circular No. 18/2020", "Circular 18/2020", "Circular No. 18 of 2020"]}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "Perquisite = FMV on the date of exercise less the exercise price, taxable in the year of exercise", "source": "OP-06 s.6", "match_any": ["exercise\\s+price", "(?:date|year)\\s+of\\s+exercise"]}, {"point": "For unlisted companies FMV is determined per Rule 3(8) by a registered merchant banker", "source": "OP-06 s.6", "match_any": ["merchant\\s+banker"]}, {"point": "Only the TDS deposit is deferred (not the taxable event), to the earliest of 48 months from the end of the relevant assessment year, sale of the shares, or cessation of employment", "source": "OP-06 s.6", "match_any": ["48\\s+months", "cessation\\s+of\\s+employment|ceases?\\s+to\\s+be\\s+(?:an\\s+)?employee"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "Deferral period runs 48 months from exercise/allotment", "patterns": ["48\\s+months\\s+from\\s+the\\s+(?:date\\s+of\\s+)?(?:exercise|allotment)"]}, {"claim": "The taxable event itself is deferred", "patterns": ["(?:perquisite|taxable\\s+event|taxation\\s+of\\s+the\\s+perquisite)\\s+(?:itself\\s+)?(?:is|stands)\\s+deferred"]}], "sources": ["tests/fixtures/opinions/OP-06_esop_taxation_startup_deferral.md"], "notes": "DRAFT from fictitious firm opinion OP-06 - expected position is that (fictitious) opinion's conclusion, not verified law. required_authorities = frontmatter authorities the opinion's Issue/Analysis/Conclusion actually relies on; frontmatter-only authorities are optional_authorities. A tax professional must confirm the position is correct law before setting verified=true.", "verified_by": "claude-draft", "verified": false}
{"id": "op07-buyback-post-oct-2024", "category": "change_in_law", "answer_mode": "research", "question": "An unlisted company proposes to buy back 5,00,000 equity shares from its promoter shareholders at INR 450 per share, with the buyback effective after 1 October 2024. Does company-level buyback tax under Section 115QA still apply, and how are the buyback proceeds taxed in the shareholders' hands?", "required_authorities": [{"id": "s115qa", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 115QA", "aliases": ["Section 115QA"], "section": "115QA"}, {"id": "s2-22-f", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 2(22)(f)", "aliases": ["Section 2(22)(f)"], "section": "2(22)(f)"}, {"id": "s56-2", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 56(2)", "aliases": ["Section 56(2)"], "section": "56(2)"}, {"id": "s194", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 194", "aliases": ["Section 194"], "section": "194"}, {"id": "finance-no2-act-2024", "kind": "other", "label": "Finance (No. 2) Act, 2024", "aliases": ["Finance (No. 2) Act, 2024", "Finance (No.2) Act, 2024", "Finance (No 2) Act 2024", "Finance Act (No. 2), 2024"]}], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "s10-34a", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 10(34A)", "aliases": ["Section 10(34A)"], "section": "10(34A)"}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "For buybacks on or after 1 October 2024 the company-level tax under Section 115QA no longer applies", "source": "OP-07 s.6-7", "match_any": ["1(?:st)?\\s+october,?\\s+2024"]}, {"point": "The entire buyback consideration is a deemed dividend under Section 2(22)(f), taxed as income from other sources under Section 56(2)", "source": "OP-07 s.6", "match_any": ["dividend", "other\\s+sources"]}, {"point": "TDS applies under Section 194", "source": "OP-07 s.6-7", "match_any": ["\\b194\\b"]}, {"point": "The shareholder's original cost of acquisition becomes a capital loss", "source": "OP-07 s.6-7", "match_any": ["capital\\s+loss"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "The company must pay buyback tax under Section 115QA", "pa