{"id": "op08-angel-tax-premium", "category": "opinion", "answer_mode": "opinion", "question": "A private company that is not DPIIT-recognised as an eligible start-up issued 10,000 compulsorily convertible preference shares to a resident angel investor at INR 1,200 per share, while its DCF valuation put fair market value at INR 950 per share. Please advise whether the excess premium is taxable under Section 56(2)(viib) and how defensible the valuation is.", "required_authorities": [{"id": "s56-2-viib", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 56(2)(viib)", "aliases": ["Section 56(2)(viib)"], "section": "56(2)(viib)"}, {"id": "rule-11ua", "kind": "rule", "label": "Rule 11UA", "aliases": ["Rule 11UA"]}, {"id": "agro-portfolio", "kind": "case", "label": "Agro Portfolio (P) Ltd v. ITO (2018)", "aliases": ["Agro Portfolio"]}], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "vbhc", "kind": "case", "label": "VBHC Value Homes (P) Ltd v. ITO", "aliases": ["VBHC Value Homes", "VBHC"]}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "Not being a recognised eligible start-up, the exemption from Section 56(2)(viib) is unavailable", "source": "OP-08 s.6", "match_any": ["(?:not|no)\\b.{0,60}(?:recogni[sz]ed|DPIIT)"]}, {"point": "Excess of INR 250 per share, INR 25 lakh in aggregate, is prima facie taxable as income from other sources", "source": "OP-08 s.6-7", "match_any": ["25\\s*lakh|25,00,000", "other\\s+sources"]}, {"point": "Per Agro Portfolio a DCF valuation is not displaced merely because actual performance diverges from projections, if assumptions were reasonable and bona fide when made", "source": "OP-08 s.6", "match_any": ["projections", "bona\\s+fide"]}, {"point": "Taxable unless the valuation is revisited or start-up recognition is obtained before allotment", "source": "OP-08 s.7", "match_any": ["before\\s+allotment|prior\\s+to\\s+allotment"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "The company is eligible for the start-up exemption", "patterns": ["(?:is|would\\s+be|will\\s+be)\\s+(?:eligible|entitled)\\s+(?