{"id": "op11-poem-mauritius", "category": "for_against", "answer_mode": "research", "question": "A Mauritius-incorporated company has three Mauritius-resident and two India-based directors. Board meetings are formally held in Mauritius, but board minutes and correspondence suggest the India-based directors substantively determine key investment and financing decisions, which the Mauritius board then ratifies. What are the arguments for and against its Place of Effective Management being in India under Section 6(3)?", "required_authorities": [{"id": "s6-3", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 6(3)", "aliases": ["Section 6(3)"], "section": "6(3)"}, {"id": "cbdt-circular-6-2017", "kind": "circular", "label": "CBDT Circular No. 6/2017 (POEM guidelines)", "aliases": ["Circular No. 6/2017", "Circular 6/2017", "Circular No. 6 of 2017"]}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "Circular 6/2017 takes a substance-over-form approach, distinguishing de jure board approval from de facto decision-making", "source": "OP-11 s.6", "match_any": ["substance\\s+over\\s+form", "de\\s+facto"]}, {"point": "Real risk that POEM is in India, exposing worldwide income to Indian tax", "source": "OP-11 s.3, s.6-7", "match_any": ["worldwide\\s+income|global\\s+income"]}, {"point": "Recommend substantively strengthening and documenting the Mauritius directors' decision-making role", "source": "OP-11 s.7", "match_any": ["strengthen"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "POEM is clearly in Mauritius / outside India", "patterns": ["POEM\\s+(?:is|lies|would\\s+be|will\\s+be)\\s+(?:clearly\\s+|firmly\\s+|safely\\s+)?(?:in\\s+Mauritius|outside\\s+India)"]}], "sources": ["tests/fixtures/opinions/OP-11_poem_mauritius_subsidiary.md"], "notes": "DRAFT from fictitious firm opinion OP-11 - expected position is that (fictitious) opinion's conclusion, not verified law. required_authorities = frontmatter authorities the opinion's Issue/Analysis/Conclusion actually relies on; frontmatter-only authorities are optional_a