{"id": "op16-80iac-imb-certification", "category": "opinion", "answer_mode": "opinion", "question": "A DPIIT-recognised start-up incorporated in FY 2022-23 develops a proprietary IoT-based soil-monitoring platform and has turnover of INR 38 crore, within the prescribed threshold, but has not yet obtained Inter-Ministerial Board certification. Please advise whether it can claim the Section 80-IAC deduction now.", "required_authorities": [{"id": "s80-iac", "kind": "section", "label": "Section 80-IAC", "aliases": ["Section 80-IAC", "80-IAC", "80IAC"], "section": "80-IAC"}], "optional_authorities": [{"id": "dpiit-gsr-127e", "kind": "other", "label": "DPIIT Notification G.S.R. 127(E)", "aliases": ["G.S.R. 127(E)", "GSR 127(E)"]}], "expected_key_points": [{"point": "Section 80-IAC is a 100% profit-linked deduction", "source": "OP-16 s.3", "match_any": ["100\\s*%"]}, {"point": "The deduction is conditional on Inter-Ministerial Board certification; DPIIT recognition alone is insufficient", "source": "OP-16 s.6", "match_any": ["inter[\\s-]ministerial\\s+board|\\bIMB\\b"]}, {"point": "Prima facie eligible, but the claim should not be made in the return until IMB certification is obtained", "source": "OP-16 s.7", "match_any": ["return\\s+of\\s+income|until.{0,60}(?:certif|IMB)"]}], "must_not_claim": [{"claim": "DPIIT recognition alone is sufficient", "patterns": ["DPIIT\\s+recognition\\s+(?:alone\\s+)?(?:is|would\\s+be)\\s+sufficient"]}, {"claim": "The deduction can be claimed now", "patterns": ["can\\s+(?:now\\s+)?claim\\s+the\\s+(?:section\\s+)?80[\\s-]?IAC\\s+deduction\\s+(?:now|immediately|in\\s+the\\s+current\\s+return)"]}], "sources": ["tests/fixtures/opinions/OP-16_startup_deduction_80IAC.md"], "notes": "DRAFT from fictitious firm opinion OP-16 - expected position is that (fictitious) opinion's conclusion, not verified law. required_authorities = frontmatter authorities the opinion's Issue/Analysis/Conclusion actually relies on; frontmatter-only authorities are optional